---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import { IELTS } from '../../../../courses/ielts/syllabus';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
---
<CourseHome course={IELTS}>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>Prepare for IELTS on your own, from start to test day</h2>
    <p>You don't need a teacher or a paid course. Every lesson teaches one thing, in order, and shows you how to practise it:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Know exactly what is coming.</strong> Every paper, every question type and every minute of the test, in plain English, with the traps that cost marks.</li>
      <li><strong>A method for every question type.</strong> True/False/Not Given, matching headings, maps, letters, Task 1 charts, Task 2 essays and the three Speaking parts, each with a worked example you can step through.</li>
      <li><strong>Model answers explained.</strong> Answers at band 6, 7 and 8 side by side, so you can see what actually changes between bands.</li>
      <li><strong>A practice room with thousands of original questions.</strong> Listening read aloud by your own device, reading passages, writing tasks with timers and word counters, and speaking cue cards. Filter by skill, Academic or General Training, question type and level.</li>
      <li><strong>Your own feedback system.</strong> Calculators for bands and Canadian CLB levels, a study planner, a mistake log and self-check lists for writing and speaking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Both modules are covered: <strong>Academic</strong> (university and professional registration) and <strong>General Training</strong> (migration and work, including Canada's Express Entry). All questions are written for fibub; none are copied from official tests. Free, no sign-up, and your progress stays in your own browser.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
